{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Cosine LR with Linear Warmup Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `CosineWithWarmup` - a stateless function `lr(step) -> float` over the configured schedule."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `TrainState` - wraps a model, an `AdamW` optimizer, and the schedule into a single step function."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `TrainState.step` - runs one forward pass, one backward pass, logs gradient L2 norm, and applies `lr(step)` to the optimizer."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `plot_schedule_ascii` - renders the schedule as a text plot the eye can read."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `write_schedule_csv` - emits one row per step with the learning rate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A demo at the bottom of the file builds a tiny `nn.Linear` model, trains for 20 steps over a fixed input batch, and prints the per-step learning rate, gradient norm, and loss. The schedule is also rendered as a text plot for the visual sanity check."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The script exits zero and prints a per-step training log plus the schedule plot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add an inverse-square-root variant of the schedule and compare it on a 200-step toy training run. Which curve produces the lower final loss?\n2. Add a `--restart` flag that adds a second warmup at `total_steps / 2`. Defend whether warm restarts improve or hurt on the toy run.\n3. Add a unit test that the schedule is continuous: for every step in `[0, total_steps]` the difference `|lr(step+1) - lr(step)|` is bounded by `lr_max / warmup_steps`.\n4. Wire the schedule into a `torch.optim.lr_scheduler.LambdaLR` so it composes with framework code. The lesson uses a plain step function; what does the wrapper change?\n5. Add a `--plot-png` flag that writes a real plot via `matplotlib`. Defend whether the lesson's text plot or the PNG is the better default for CI runs."
      ]
    }
  ],
